{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And for inside the parochet.</b> From here they said: there was a place behind the parochet where they would examine records of priestly lineage." "<b>Service of gift.</b> Just as a gift is with appeasement, so too the service is with appeasement. Rashi explained here: <b>a gift</b> — I have given it to you, that is, they should not say, 'you entered it of your own accord.'" "<b>And the stranger who approaches.</b> For service, even in purity, and even a Levite — he shall be put to death. And one should not raise an objection from Samuel the Ramatite, who offered and was only a Levite, because it was a temporary ruling, like that of Gideon. <b>The stranger who approaches shall die</b> — the punishment we have heard; the warning, from where? The verse says: <b>a stranger shall not approach among you.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:28.132019568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}